ompensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 372 people. Revenue per employee of $192K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers, improving at 13%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $50K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Spire Global, Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $338M market cap on $72M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -4% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -51% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 50%.","The company is burning through $93M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +52.7% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -12.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 26% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 6.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Accruals elevated at +52.7% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-2.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Beneish M-Score flags potential earnings manipulation \u2014 a question